Feature: Calculate Applied Quantity for Inventory Transactions
  In order to manage and track inventory allocations effectively
  As a user in the Life Sciences sector
  I want to calculate applied quantity (apl_qty) based on specific transactional and cumulative fields

  Background:
    Given the table "purgo_playground.purgo_playground.f_inv_movmnt_apl_qty" exists
    And it contains transactional data fields

  Scenario Outline: Calculate Applied Quantity for Inventory Movements
    Given the transaction data:
      | txn_id | ref_txn_qty | cumulative_txn_qty | cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty | ref_ord_sched_qty | prior_cumulative_txn_qty | prior_cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty |
      | <txn_id> | <ref_txn_qty> | <cumulative_txn_qty> | <cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty> | <ref_ord_sched_qty> | <prior_cumulative_txn_qty> | <prior_cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty> |
    When I calculate apl_qty based on conditions
    Then the calculated apl_qty should be <apl_qty>

    Examples:
      | txn_id | ref_txn_qty | cumulative_txn_qty | cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty | ref_ord_sched_qty | prior_cumulative_txn_qty | prior_cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty | apl_qty |
      | 1      | 50.0        | 100.0              | 90.0                         | 50.0              | 40.0                     | 30.0                               | 50.0    |
      | 2      | -10.0       | 80.0               | 70.0                         | 40.0              | 50.0                     | 45.0                               | -10.0   |
      | 3      | 20.0        | 60.0               | 100.0                        | 30.0              | 30.0                     | 25.0                               | 20.0    |

  Scenario: Condition 1 - ref_txn_qty > 0 and cumulative_txn_qty >= cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty
    Given ref_txn_qty is greater than 0
    And cumulative_txn_qty is greater than or equal to cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty
    When prior_cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty is less than prior_cumulative_txn_qty
    Then set apl_qty to ref_ord_sched_qty minus difference between prior_cumulative_txn_qty and prior_cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty
    Otherwise, use ref_ord_sched_qty as apl_qty

  Scenario: Condition 2 - ref_txn_qty > 0 and cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty >= cumulative_txn_qty
    Given ref_txn_qty is greater than 0
    And cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty is greater than or equal to cumulative_txn_qty
    When prior_cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty is greater than prior_cumulative_txn_qty
    Then set apl_qty to ref_txn_qty minus difference between prior_cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty and prior_cumulative_txn_qty
    Otherwise, use ref_txn_qty as apl_qty

  Scenario: Condition 3 - ref_txn_qty < 0 and cumulative_txn_qty != 0 and cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty > 0
    Given ref_txn_qty is less than 0
    And cumulative_txn_qty is not equal to 0
    And cumulative_ref_ord_sched_qty is greater than 0
    Then set apl_qty to ref_txn_qty

  Scenario: Default Condition - none of the above conditions met
    Given none of the above conditions are met
    Then set apl_qty to NULL

  Scenario: Validate Error Conditions
    Given invalid data types for fields
    Then output error message "Invalid data format"
